Subject: [PATCH 25/37] Present sheets, covers, alerts and dialogs on Linux

A presented view travels up as a preference to a host at the root of the
scene, which shows it over the app with the environment of the view that
presented it, and dismiss for it. Sheets rest at their detents, show a
drag indicator and close on a drag down; fullScreenCover covers the
screen and popover is a sheet, as on an iPhone. Alerts and confirmation
dialogs draw as on iOS, a dialog with its cancel button apart; an action
dismisses them. The Alert and ActionSheet structures work through them.
